{
  "requirement": "The method is declared under {cite}`requirements.sdk.graph.running-criteria.load_evidence`.\n\n`load_evidence` captures the source identity and criterion path while constructing\nits future. It retains no reference to the criterion value while storage is\npending, so the criterion needs no `Sync` bound. It loads the complete record and\ndecodes its output under {cite}`requirements.sdk.graph.evidence.record.output`.\nVersion and input comparison are separate steps.",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "The reviewed tests cover every obligation in `check_node`.\n\n**Capture and no `Sync` bound.**\n- `validation_and_answer_need_send_without_sync` in `tests/contracts.rs` wraps `validator.load_evidence(&descriptor)` in `send(..)`, where `fn send<T: Send>`.\n- The `Review` criterion holds a `Cell` field (`descriptor_reads`), so it is not `Sync`.\n- A future that kept a reference to it while storage was pending would not be `Send`, and the test would fail to compile.\n- That test also asserts `descriptor.descriptor_reads.get() == 1`. The criterion's `source_node_id` is read exactly once. This is consistent with capturing source and path at construction.\n\n**Complete record loading.**\n- `criteria_keep_typed_answers_and_persist_only_when_requested` stores a record and loads it back. It checks the output, source, path, version and dependencies, and that the output is stored unchanged.\n- `changing_one_criteria_input_does_not_invalidate_another` and `dependency_resolution_failures_do_not_execute_or_replace_saved_answers` check that loaded dependencies equal the saved ones.\n\n**Missing and wrong-identity records.**\n- `Ok(None)` is asserted in `criteria_keep_typed_answers_and_persist_only_when_requested`.\n- `wildcard_revision_does_not_supply_other_criteria_or_nodes` asserts `None` for a different criterion path and a different source node.\n- `caller_reuses_negative_answers_and_compares_revisions_explicitly` asserts `None` for a different node.\n\n**Output decoding (`record.output`).**\n- `typed_loading_reports_decode_errors_even_for_stale_evidence` asserts `ValidationError::Output` for undecodable output. It does so with both a changed version and stale dependencies, and checks that no input reads happen.\n- `malformed_records_are_storage_errors_and_bad_outputs_are_output_errors` asserts `ValidationError::Output` for a bad output with an obsolete version. It checks the stored file is unchanged.\n- The same test asserts that a malformed file gives `ValidationError::Graph(FileStorageError::Json(_))`.\n- `loading_execution_resolution_and_saving_failures_do_not_publish_answers` and `resolution_storage_and_callback_errors_are_not_judgments` assert `ValidationError::Graph(\"load\")` for a storage failure.\n\n**Version and input comparison are separate steps.**\n- In `caller_reuses_negative_answers_and_compares_revisions_explicitly`, loading with a `v2` criterion returns the `v1` record. Compatibility is then checked separately with `is_compatible_with`.\n- The same test covers the legacy case where the record's version is `None`.\n- `wildcard_revision_does_not_supply_other_criteria_or_nodes` covers a record with no version loaded under a different revision.\n- `dependency_resolution_failures_do_not_execute_or_replace_saved_answers` loads successfully while input resolution is failing. `check_inputs` then returns the error separately.\n- `changing_one_criteria_input_does_not_invalidate_another` loads records whose inputs changed. `check_inputs` is `false` for one and `true` for the other.\n\nNo gap found.",
  "references": "37b76c66e8d4cd2f6e9436578c3dd3b480409945a5727e53d405807d6c6e2867",
